    "summary_one_sentence": "A 40-year-old advertising executive attempts to revitalize his flagging career by joining a wild Miami bachelor party after being mistakenly added to a group chat of twentysomethings.",
    "summary_short": "Facing a career crisis, a 40-year-old advertising executive gets an unexpected lifeline when he is accidentally added to a group chat of twentysomethings planning a Miami bachelor party. Seeing a rare opportunity to connect with a younger demographic and save his job, he decides to join the wild weekend getaway. As chaos ensues over 72 hours, he must navigate generation gaps, high-stakes partying, and his own hidden motives. Ultimately, the unpredictable journey forces him to redefine success, friendship, and what it truly means to grow up.",
    "summary_long": "Desperate to stay relevant in a rapidly changing industry, a 40-year-old advertising executive finds his career hanging by a thread as his agency favors younger voices. His life takes a comedic twist when he is mistakenly added to a vibrant group chat of twentysomethings planning an outrageous bachelor party in Miami. Recognizing a golden chance to understand the youth culture his pitch decks desperately need, he leaps at the opportunity and joins the trip. What begins as an awkward intrusion quickly devolves into 72 hours of unpredictable mayhem, sun-drenched chaos, and wild partying across South Beach. Throughout the weekend, the generational divide becomes glaringly obvious, leading to both hilarious misunderstandings and poignant personal friction. However, as the crew faces various wild mishaps, the executive begins to offer grounded wisdom while absorbing the energetic spontaneity of his young companions. He slowly earns their trust, forming unexpected bonds that transcend age differences and professional ambition. By the end of the trip, he realizes that saving his career isn't about faking youth, but about embracing authenticity. He returns home not only with a renewed perspective on his life and work, but with genuine friendships born out of 72 unforgettable hours.",
    "synopsis": "\"72 HOURS\" is a lighthearted comedy-drama that explores age gaps, professional desperation, and unexpected camaraderie. When a struggling 40-year-old ad executive is accidentally included in a group text for a wild Miami bachelor party, he seizes the opportunity to immerse himself in the youth culture he has lost touch with. Joining the crew of twentysomethings for three days of chaotic partying, he attempts to bridge the generational divide in a bid to save his job. Across a whirlwind weekend of sun, beach, and party-fueled mishaps, both he and the group learn valuable lessons about connection, identity, and the humor found in life's unscripted moments.",
